How to mount or map s3 bucket inside the docker image?

Ans : Use s3fs to Mount S3 Bucket as Filesystem

s3fs allows you to mount an S3 bucket as a local filesystem, which you can then mount into a Docker container.

Steps:
1.Install s3fs on the host system:

sudo apt-get install s3fs  # for Ubuntu/Debian

2.Store your AWS credentials:

echo ACCESS_KEY:SECRET_KEY > ~/.passwd-s3fs
chmod 600 ~/.passwd-s3fs

3. Create a mount point and mount the S3 bucket:

mkdir ~/s3bucket
s3fs your-bucket-name ~/s3bucket -o passwd_file=~/.passwd-s3fs

4.Run Docker and mount the directory:

docker run -v ~/s3bucket:/mnt/s3bucket my-image
